[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture decisions

[DECISION]
UID: ETH-SYA-200
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: SPI Ethernet controller W5500
CONTEXT: ESP32-S3 has no EMAC/RMII. J7 only offers SPI.
DECISION: Use the W5500 (SPI, integrated PHY and TCP/IP offload).
CONSEQUENCES: >>>
Supported by ESPHome and Arduino ETH. Throughput limited by SPI, sufficient
for the application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-003

[DECISION]
UID: ETH-SYA-201
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Supply from the main board 3.3 V
CONTEXT: >>>
The AMS1117 path (JP5) needs about 1 V headroom behind the diode OR and drops
out at about 0.9 Ohm slot resistance.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Use JP4 (3.3 V from the main board step-down converter) as default; U2 becomes
an assembly option.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-011

[DECISION]
UID: ETH-SYA-202
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: W5500 reset on J7 pin 6
CONTEXT: >>>
J7 has no dedicated reset pin. v1.x routed pin 6 through the PCA9306, which
gated the reset with I2C_EXT_EN.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Use J7 pin 6 (SDA) as W5500 RSTn. With the PCA9306 removed in v2.0 the host
drives it directly from GPIO16.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: >>>
I2C on J7 cannot be used together with the extension (I2C traffic would pulse
RSTn).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ETH-SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-204

[[/SECTION]]
